    {
      "itemId": "ENG-025-LW-09",
      "verdict": "HOLD",
      "faultAt": [
        "question",
        "option That it is hard to forgive the loss of the book.",
        "option That she was very naughty."
      ],
      "fault": "The question asks what Meg tells Amy to WAIT FOR. Two distractors (\"That it is hard to forgive the loss of the book.\", \"That she was very naughty.\") are that-clauses that cannot complete \"wait for ...\", so the question's own wording rules them out, and \"Until Laurie has gone off home...\" also does not fit \"wait for\". Only the key (\"A quiet minute once Jo has cheered up.\") is a thing one can wait for, so it is singled out by grammar, not by reading lines 53 to 54.",
      "objective": false,
      "suggestedFix": "Ask \"What does Meg tell Amy to do?\" or recast every distractor as a moment or event Amy could wait for."
    },
